, integrating hyper heuristic-based feature selection, and fuzzy deep learning. Initially, the relevance of input features is assessed to reduce dimensionality and highlight the most informative biomarkers characteristics. Multiple optimization algorithms are applied iteratively to identify an optimal subset of features (WHH), ensuring efficient exploration of the search space. The selected features are subsequently processed by a lightweight fuzzy deep learning model, which captures complex patterns while maintaining interpretability. This approach balances predictive performance with computational efficiency, and it is designed to produce explainable results that can support clinical decision-making without introducing subjective bias. The proposed WHFDL model is illustrated in the flowchart below (Fig.
